WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.110
- All right, let's finish up

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:04.080
with one last story that
celebrates our love of reading.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.178
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.178 --> 00:00:07.890
(rock music)

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.590
Everyone in our audience is
holding a book in their hands

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.170
and there's something about
a real book, not a tablet,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.660
that makes reading that
much more enjoyable.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.493
Don't you agree?

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:17.326
It's a real book.

00:00:17.326 --> 00:00:18.159
It's tangible, it's nice.

00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:19.440
It smells good, it's nice.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.273
Every year though,

00:00:20.273 --> 00:00:22.620
there are fewer librarians
working in public schools.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.380
In fact, there are fewer
libraries in schools at all.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.990
So a Nebraska nonprofit is
working to put physical books

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.230
in the hands of every school
kid whenever they want one.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.660
It's called DIBS for Kids,
and it recently won an award

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.104
from the Library of Congress.

00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:35.937
(imitating siren)

00:00:35.937 --> 00:00:37.350
(audience cheering)
Here to explain,

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.780
let's say hi to Angie watching on KETV.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:40.948
What's up, Angie?

00:00:40.948 --> 00:00:42.210
(audience cheering)

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.500
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.333
- Hello.

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:45.780
So this isn't a library.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.640
Can you explain how it works?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.320
- Yeah, so DIBS for Kids,

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.830
which stands for Delivering
Infinite Bookshelves for Kids,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:56.790
provides high interest,
representative, diverse books

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.800
in elementary schools throughout Omaha.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.530
We work with 5,000 students here.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.440
And what we do, like you
can see in this picture,

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.930
students every day come
into their classroom

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.410
pick out a physical, tangible
book, take it home to read,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.570
come back the next day,
check that book in,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.670
pick out another book for themselves.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.530
And that means that, you know,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.390
the kids can discover the joy of reading.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.700
They take home about three
books a week on average,

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.840
and we're just thrilled to be

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.370
on that reading journey with them.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.990
- It's really incredible
what you're doing.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.783
There's a lot of ground
to cover though, right?

00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:30.060
- There is a significant
amount of ground to cover.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.110
Like you said, libraries are
every year there's fewer,

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:34.943
but you know what?

00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:37.740
We know that bringing
more books into classrooms

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.260
lets kids really experience
that joy of reading.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:44.520
We know it helps kids gain
further reading proficiency,

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.380
get back up to grade level.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.740
And so, really being able
to be in the classrooms

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.768
really helps DIBS and
those students specifically

00:01:52.768 --> 00:01:55.440
can make up all of that ground.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.400
And like I said,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.470
we just are so thrilled to be able

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.590
to help all of those students
here in the Omaha community.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.760
- Well, it's incredible.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.920
It's amazing what you're
doing for all those kids.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.270
Thank you so much, Angie.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.024
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:08.024 --> 00:02:08.857
(audience clapping)

00:02:08.857 --> 00:02:10.200
- [Angie] Yeah, thank you so much.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.400
I appreciate it.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.020
- Absolutely, and that's not all, girl.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.520
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.230
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.490
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.130
want to celebrate those
instilling the love of reading

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.570
to all just like you

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.790
so they're giving DIBS for Kids $1,000.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.623
How's that sound?

00:02:24.623 --> 00:02:25.747
- Ah, thank you.

00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:27.000
Thank you so much.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.833
That's amazing.

00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:28.710
We appreciate it.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.730
- Absolutely, Angie.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:30.563
Have a great day

00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:32.220
and thank you to all of
our guests this hour.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.740
Jane Fonda, Candice Bergen, Diane Keaton,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.720
Mary Steenburgen, and Caitlin Smith.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.824
Y'all have a great day and if it's not,

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:40.743
maybe get lost in a book and
try and make the day better.

